Title:
Defender Bender Box

Type:
GitHub Tool

Short Summary (4-8 sentences max):
Defender Bender Box is a local research utility that runs the x64 Microsoft Defender scan engine offline inside a Linux Docker container via Wine to test whether a file triggers a static Defender detection and what threat name is returned. It solves the need for repeatable, isolated “does Defender flag this file?” checks without executing the sample, by mounting the target read-only and feeding it to the engine through read callbacks. The project directly loads `mpengine.dll`, boots it via `__rsignal`, and performs a stream scan using pinned VDM definition files, avoiding the `MsMpEng.exe`/`MpCmdRun.exe` service path that fails under Wine due to ALPC/RPC endpoint issues. It outputs smoke logs plus a concise report including scan counts, callback flags, and candidate threat name when a detection callback fires. It’s useful for red teamers, pentesters, and malware analysts doing preflight testing of payloads against Defender’s offline signatures, and for defenders validating static detection behavior in a controlled environment. The key caveat is that “no detection” is reported as UNVERIFIED (not a clean verdict) and cloud/behavioral protections are out of scope.

Technical Focus:
- Running Windows Defender engine (`mpengine.dll`) under Wine in Docker
- Direct engine initialization via `__rsignal` and callback-driven scanning
- VDM definition handling (`mpavbase/mpavdlta/mpasbase/mpasdlta`)
- Isolation controls (disposable containers, read-only mounts, `--network none`)
- Harness/loader shims (WdFilter and ETW compatibility)

Use Cases:
- Offline static signature testing of red team payloads and droppers
- Reproducing/triaging Defender threat-name classifications for samples
- Regression testing against a pinned Defender engine/definition set
- Building a local “AV scan oracle” for research workflows without sample execution

Keywords:
Microsoft Defender, mpengine.dll, VDM, mpavbase.vdm, mpavdlta.vdm, mpasbase.vdm, mpasdlta.vdm, Wine, Docker, offline scanning, static detection, __rsignal, detection callback, stream scan, ALPC, RPC endpoint, WdFilter, ETW, EICAR, malware analysis